Residual risk: `??` only guards `null`/`undefined`, so all 4 UNCLEAR sites (and any site using the canonical pattern with an *invalid* string, e.g. `tools/serve.mjs:15` with `PORT="abc"`) can still produce `NaN` — the canonical fix is necessary but not sufficient; a `Number.isFinite` guard after coercion is the complete fix.
Of the swept sites, 13/26 are direct `??`-after-coercion BUGs, but only `src/worker.js:214` sits on a JSON response body, so only that one can reproduce the exact `/promote` `NaN → null` symptom today.
The nearest second-order risk is `quilt-gpu-lab/experiments/engine.mjs:77` (`dt`) and `:81` (`sub`): both feed numeric fields that the harness echoes back in its result object, so if those results are ever serialized they would emit `null` exactly as `/promote` did.
`superinstance-api/scripts/report.mjs:62` is the other latent `NaN → null` path — it re-coerces already-parsed row data with `+r.score`, bypassing any fix applied upstream.
Everything else in the BUG set degrades to a `NaN` loop bound/count (hangs or no-ops) rather than a `null` in JSON, so severity is lower but the default value is silently discarded in all 13 cases.
Recommended follow-up: apply the PATCH.diff hunk to `src/worker.js:214`, then mechanically rewrite the remaining 12 BUG sites to the parenthesized `+(get(k) ?? default)` form and add `Number.isFinite` validation at the 4 UNCLEAR sites.
